  "name": "B TYPE NATRIUTERIC PEPTIDE (BNP)",
  "code": "1045",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>BNP concentration in patients of Heart failure.</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9989%; height: 134.453px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 33.2869%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.2869%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.2869%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td><strong>NYHA CLASSES&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>5TH -95TH PERCENTILE</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&gt;100 pg/mL (%)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>I&nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&lt;2-772</td>\n<td>43.1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>II&nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\n<td>5.4-999</td>\n<td>58.7</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.6133px;\">\n<td>III&nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\n<td>21.1-1696</td>\n<td>82.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>IV&nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\n<td>109-3157</td>\n<td>95.8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>ALL&nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\n<td>10.8-1873</td>\n<td>72.6</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Comments</strong><br>BNP is stored mainly in the myocardium and has biologic effects similar to those of Atrial Natriuretic Peptide (ANP). Increased concentrations of BNP occur in patients with hypervolemic states like congestive heart failure &amp; hypertension. The circulating&nbsp;levels of BNP directly correlate with the higher incidence of cardiac events and mortality in patients with heart failure.</p>\n<p><strong>Increased Levels</strong></p>\n<p><br>Cardiac causes: Heart failure, Asymptomatic Left ventricular dysfunction, Arterial &amp; Pulmonary hypertension, Cardiac&nbsp;hypertrophy, Valvular heart disease, Arrhythmia, Acute Coronary syndrome</p>\n<p><br>Non Cardiac causes: Acute &amp; Chronic renal failure, Liver Cirrhosis, Hyperaldosteronism, Cushing&rsquo;s syndrome</p>\n<p><br><strong>Clinical Uses</strong></p>\n<p><br>To confirm heart failure in patients presenting with ambiguous clinical symptoms.<br>To assist / improve diagnostic accuracy for heart failure.</p>",
